        "execSummary":  "Google\u0027s I/O 2026 keynote marks the company\u0027s most explicit statement yet that the AI competitive era has shifted from model benchmarks to agentic platforms ΓÇö the ability to deploy AI that acts autonomously on behalf of users over extended time horizons. For enterprise AI strategists, the scale numbers are the real signal: $180-190B in annual infrastructure spend and 3.2 quadrillion monthly tokens processed means Google is building for a future where AI agent workloads dwarf current LLM inference volumes by orders of magnitude. The Gemini Spark personal agent running 24/7 on dedicated cloud infrastructure is a direct bet that the next platform war is won by whoever owns the always-on AI layer between users and information. Enterprise leaders should factor this agentic infrastructure trajectory into vendor lock-in assessments and long-term AI platform decisions.",
        "vendorLean":  "Google",
        "imageUrl":  "https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/SundarKeynote-hero.width-200.format-webp.webp"
