        "execSummary":  "Enterprises moving agentic AI from pilot to production consistently run into the same blocker: how do you control what agents can access and do at scale without manual oversight of every action? This maturity model gives enterprise architects a concrete, incremental path to answer that question using AWS-native tooling. For customer-support and operations leaders, Scope 2\u0027s identity-aware authorization and data scrubbing capabilities are particularly relevant ΓÇö they enable agents to take action on behalf of specific users while limiting exposure of sensitive records. The implicit commitment here is to AWS\u0027s ecosystem; organizations with multi-cloud or hybrid strategies should evaluate how portable these governance patterns are outside of Bedrock.",
