        "summary":  "ADOP is a reference architecture on Amazon Bedrock that uses specialized AI agents to automate data pipeline creation across Bronze-Silver-Gold lakehouse layers, reducing weeks of manual work to hours. Agents generate ETL code, quality checks, semantic models, and compliance controls at build time, producing deterministic artifacts that run in production without runtime model dependencies.",
        "execSummary":  "ADOP represents a meaningful shift in how enterprises can approach data engineering bottlenecks: rather than waiting weeks for human data engineers to build and validate pipelines, agentic AI handles the scaffolding automatically and hands off deterministic code ΓÇö not live model calls ΓÇö to production. For enterprise AI leaders, the architecture\u0027s separation of build-time AI from runtime execution addresses a key concern about reliability and auditability in regulated environments. Customer-support and operations teams sitting on large unstructured data sets may find this particularly relevant as a path to faster analytics and reporting pipelines. The reference architecture is AWS-specific, and the claimed time compression should be validated against your organization\u0027s data complexity before planning around it.",
