        "execSummary":  "The scale of this announcement ΓÇö 4.25 gigawatts, $150-200 billion per upgrade cycle ΓÇö signals that AI compute infrastructure is transitioning from technology investment to strategic national asset, with implications for where and how enterprise AI capacity will be available over the next decade. For enterprise leaders planning long-horizon AI strategy, the concentration of frontier compute in a small number of hyperscale facilities raises both availability and geopolitical risk questions that should factor into infrastructure planning. The financial partnership model involving major institutional investors suggests that AI compute is being institutionalized as a regulated asset class, which may affect pricing and access dynamics for enterprise buyers. This is primarily a real estate and infrastructure story; direct operational implications for most enterprise AI programs are indirect and long-term.",
