        "summary":  "Researchers from Harvard Business School, MIT, and the University of Washington found that AI-generated explanations can suppress independent human judgment. When evaluators received LLM rationales alongside recommendations, they were more likely to defer to incorrect AI decisions and reject promising ideas.",
        "execSummary":  "Enterprise leaders deploying AI decision-support tools face a counterintuitive risk: the more clearly AI explains its reasoning, the less critically employees may evaluate those recommendations. A multi-university study found that AI-generated explanations increased deference to wrong AI outputs and suppressed human creativity. For customer-support and operations leaders, this means explanation features may degrade quality rather than improve it when agents stop second-guessing the system. Governance frameworks should include explicit protocols for human override and critical challenge of AI-recommended actions.",
